/question-capture-workers/linear/14040091/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c099b8a5af4bbe1931dab27ba587dfa4139b4f6d569435d89c682c6fc59f037"} {"question" "q-91160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries below ${a}_{13}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -2 & 5 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 18 & 0 \\\\ 5 & -8 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}2 & -4 & 1 \\\\ -7 & 18 & 0 \\\\ -13 & 28 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-9{R}_{1}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040091/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c099b8a5af4bbe1931dab27ba587dfa4139b4f6d569435d89c682c6fc59f037"} {"question" "q-91160" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040091/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9621d434515595164b9a7b82a0b62acb60abf05f431523c0f0f85bd07935f033"} {"question" "q-91160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040091/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c099b8a5af4bbe1931dab27ba587dfa4139b4f6d569435d89c682c6fc59f037"} {"question" "q-91160" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+5{R}_{1}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+9{R}_{1}$"] ["text" "$