gin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-3 & 0 & -5 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040091/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c099b8a5af4bbe1931dab27ba587dfa4139b4f6d569435d89c682c6fc59f037"} {"question" "q-42531" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040091/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "9621d434515595164b9a7b82a0b62acb60abf05f431523c0f0f85bd07935f033"} {"question" "q-42531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040091/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c099b8a5af4bbe1931dab27ba587dfa4139b4f6d569435d89c682c6fc59f037"} {"question" "q-42531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3}$"] ["text" "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}$"] ["text" "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{3}$"] ["text" "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+{R}_{3}$"] ["text" "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040091/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c099b8a5af4bbe1931dab27ba587dfa4139b4f6d569435d89c682c6fc59f037"} {"question" "q-42531" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}$"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040091/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c099b8a5af4bbe1931dab27ba587dfa4139b4f6d569435d89c682c6fc59f037"} {"question" "q-91162" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{3},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040091/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c099b8a5af4bbe1931dab27ba587dfa4139b4f6d569435d89c682c6fc59f037"} {"question" "q-91162" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above ${a}_{31}=1$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -4 & -3 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & -12 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 8 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}0 & -5 & -12 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -10 \\\\ 1 & 1 & 9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{3}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14040091/state.json" "file_sha256" "4c099b8a5af4bbe1931dab27ba587